Period Hygiene: 10 Simple Tips Every Woman Should Know

Periods are a normal part of life, and maintaining good menstrual hygiene can make those days more comfortable and manageable. You do not need a complicated routine. A few simple habits can help you stay clean, comfortable, and confident throughout your period.

1. Change Your Pad Regularly

Do not wait until your pad is completely saturated. Check it regularly and change it according to your flow and comfort. Heavy-flow days may require more frequent changes.

2. Wash Your Hands

Always wash your hands before and after changing your sanitary pad. It is one of the easiest ways to maintain good hygiene.

3. Keep the Area Clean

Clean the external genital area gently with water as part of your normal hygiene routine. Avoid excessive scrubbing or heavily fragranced products if they cause irritation.

4. Select the Right Pad

Different menstrual days may require different levels of protection. A regular pad may be suitable for light flow, while longer and more absorbent pads can be useful for heavier flow.

